[size=5][color=#B8860B][b]Vivid World — A Life of Their Own[/b][/color][/size]

Do the lords and wanderers of Calradia feel like they have no lives of their own, just heartless quest dispensers?
Does talking to NPCs feel pointless?
[b]Vivid World sets out to fix that, and to make Calradia a living, breathing land![/b]
NPCs now have lives of their own: they quarrel, scheme for power, gossip, make friends and make enemies.
And now you can be part of their stories: go around picking up news, get to know each person's character, or solve a mystery. Yes, NPCs will even make up lies to get what they want.


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]What is in so far[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]New events:[/b] 20,000 words of new events, and each NPC's character can send them in a different direction: some become friends over them, some become enemies, and some keep it to themselves until the right moment to let it out.
[*][b]Rumors:[/b] NPCs pass on what happened to themselves and to others by word of mouth, but not every retelling gets every detail across. To find out what really happened, you will need to talk to a few people. [color=#D9534F][b]Note: not every NPC is willing to tell just anyone. You may need to be on good terms with them.[/b][/color]
[*][b]Rumor mode:[/b] choose Casual or Realistic in MCM to decide how willing NPCs are to open up to you as a stranger. By default it is picked automatically based on the mods you have installed.
[*][b]Memory:[/b] NPCs remember what happened, and they forget. A small, unimportant matter may be forgotten within a few days.
[*][b]Opinions:[/b] just like in real life, the news an NPC hears changes how they see the people in it.
[*][b]Grudges:[/b] on top of the game's own relations, the mod keeps its own ledger of grudges. Events and rumors leave people with scores to settle, so two people can be on good terms and still have bad blood between them. When the one holding the grudge is a clan leader or a leader's close family, a personal grudge can grow into a feud between the two clans, and the two clan leaders' relation changes with it.
[*][b]Personal relations:[/b] (inspired by Affairs of Calradia) the base game's clan-to-clan relations become person-to-person, so you get to have a real relationship with each NPC.
[*][b]False rumors:[/b] NPCs may spread lies to get ahead, or just for fun? From making up good deeds for their own family to accusing an enemy of poisoning someone to death. The person talked about may come forward to deny it, and those who know the truth may set the record straight.
[*][b]Their own judgment:[/b] NPCs decide for themselves whether to believe what they hear, and whether to pass it on. With you, they also hold back or open up depending on how they feel about you and on their character.
[*][b]Chronicle:[/b] Ctrl+L (by default, can be changed) opens the chronicle, which keeps every piece of news you have heard and marks "Conflicting accounts" when what you heard does not add up. If you fancy yourself a detective, check it often ;)
[*][b]Asking around:[/b] ask an NPC about something you have already heard, and see whether they tell it differently. Maybe what you heard first was not true after all?
[*][b]What happens in the game:[/b] what actually happens in the game becomes news too, such as captures, releases, escapes, births, deaths and marriages.
[*][b]Everyone tells it their own way:[/b] after passing on a piece of news, an NPC adds what they think of it. The same story sounds different from a friend of the person involved, an enemy and a bystander, and people telling their own story speak with their own feelings.
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Planned[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Caught up in it:[/b] you may witness events between NPCs, or even get drawn into them.
[*][b]More events[/b]
[*][b]Real effects on the game:[/b] for now events are only stories; apart from relations, no numbers change. The hope is to tie them into the game so these events become "real".
[*][b]Your turn to talk:[/b] talk your way around, set people against each other, and throw the whole continent into chaos? What a troublemaker ;)
[*][b]More sources of news:[/b] events from other mods brought into this one.
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Installation[/b][/color][/size]

[b]Game version:[/b] built against [b]v1.4.8[/b]. Other versions are untested.

[list=1]
[*]Extract and place the whole VividWorld folder into the game's Modules\ directory.
[*][color=#D9534F][b]Install Mod Configuration Menu (MCM) as well[/b][/color], loaded before this mod.
[*]Tick [b]Vivid World[/b] in the launcher, after Native, SandBoxCore, Sandbox and StoryMode.
[*]Harmony does not need to be installed separately.
[/list]

[b]Uninstalling:[/b] delete the module folder. Back up your saves first.


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Save safety[/b][/color][/size]

The rumor data is [b]not written into your save files[/b]. It lives in
Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\VividWorld\

[list]
[*][b]Remove the mod and your existing saves still load.[/b] The personal relations recorded by "Personal relations" stay in the save, but the base game does not read them, and the screen goes back to the value a clan shares from its leader.
[*][b]Move a save to another machine and the rumours do not follow[/b] — copy that folder as well.
[*][b]Load an older save and the rumors go back to that point too.[/b] Every save keeps a snapshot of the rumors; press F9 (by default, can be changed) to see them and clear out the ones whose saves you have already deleted.
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Compatibility[/b][/color][/size]

[b]Mods where commoners may not address nobles[/b] (NaN, Lowborn and the like): Vivid World detects them and, with the rumor mode on Auto, switches to Realistic, limiting asking for news to clan tier 1 and above. At tier 0 you will get nothing, and that is deliberate; to let a commoner ask anyway, switch to Casual.

[b]Calradia Remembers[/b]: Vivid World is currently integrated with Calradia Remembers only. With it installed, when you chat with a lord or wanderer through AI, he knows the rumors he has heard in Vivid World and still remembers — in the version he heard, and he can say who told him; what he has forgotten or what is long out of date does not come up. Other AI chat mods do not receive these rumors yet; without Calradia Remembers, nothing in Vivid World is affected. The language used for this is set in the "AI Integration" group in MCM (English by default).

[b]Mods that take over a lord's opening line:[/b] some mods claim the first thing a lord says. When that happens, an extra line appears in the dialogue menu — "You looked like you had something to say?" — to bring the subject back.

[b]Affairs of Calradia[/b]: with its personal relations mode on, it does the same thing as "Personal relations", and the two do not conflict; Vivid World detects that it is already being done and does not redistribute relations.

Apart from "Personal relations" changing how the game computes someone's relation with you, Vivid World does not change the game's own AI decisions and overwrites no native files.


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Settings[/b][/color][/size]

[b]There is a Vivid World page in the game's settings screen[/b] (provided by Mod Configuration Menu), all changeable in game.

The settings file lives at Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\VividWorld\config.json and is created the first time you run the game — the master switch, the hotkeys, how many snapshots to keep, and more. Both routes write the same file, and settings not on the page are left untouched.

[b]Updating the mod never changes settings you have altered[/b] — only missing keys are added.


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Languages[/b][/color][/size]

English, Traditional Chinese and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/13594]Russian[/url] are included. More languages are welcome.
[list]
[*]Thanks to Lingaraja for the Russian localization!
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Reporting problems[/b][/color][/size]

The log is at Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\VividWorld\log.txt — please attach it. If the problem is about who told what to whom, set debug.logTellerTurns to true in config.json, restart, reproduce it, and the log will say a great deal more.


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]Note[/b][/color][/size]

This is my first mod, and I use AI (Claude) to develop. Feel free to leave a comment or report a bug on Nexus, or if you would like to contribute to this mod, you can visit my [url=https://github.com/PH010546/VividWorld]github repo[/url].


[line]

[size=5][color=#B8860B][b]鮮活世界：各有其道（Vivid World）[/b][/color][/size]

你是否覺得卡拉迪亞的領主及流浪者沒有自己的生活、僅是一個無情的任務交辦機器？
你是否覺得與NPC對話沒有任何意義？
[b]Vivid World旨在解決這些困擾，意圖打造一個活生生的卡拉迪亞大陸！[/b]
現在，NPC們會有自己的生活：會和他人吵架、會爭權奪利、會討論八卦、會與人交好或結仇。
而你現在可以參與他們的故事，四處打聽新的消息、了解這個角色的個性，或是解謎──對，NPC們甚至會為了特定目的編造謊言。


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]目前已經實作的機制[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]模組新增的事件：[/b]兩萬字的新事件，並會依照每個NPC不同的個性導致可能不同的走向──有人會因為事件交好，也有人會因此結仇；甚至有人會偷偷藏在心底，等到特定時刻才說出口。
[*][b]傳聞機制：[/b]NPC會透過口耳相傳，把自己或他人所發生的事傳遞出去，但不是每次都可以準確地將所有資訊轉達。為了了解事件真相，你需要多找幾個人聊聊天。[color=#D9534F][b]注意：不是每個NPC都願意跟任何人訴說，你可能要與他們足夠友好。[/b][/color]
[*][b]傳聞模式：[/b]可在MCM選擇「暢玩」或「寫實」，決定NPC對陌生的你有多願意開口。預設會依你裝的模組自動選擇。
[*][b]記憶系統：[/b]NPC會記住事件，也會忘記。不重要的小事可能過幾天就忘了。
[*][b]好感系統：[/b]如同現實一般，NPC聽到的消息會改變他們對當事人的看法。
[*][b]恩怨系統：[/b]除了遊戲內建的好感度，模組引入了自己的恩怨帳本。每個人會因為事件或傳聞而有恩怨，所以可能會有「關係友好但有嫌隙」的情況發生。如果結下恩怨的是族長或族長的至親，個人恩怨還可能升級成家族恩怨，兩家族長之間的好感也會跟著改變。
[*][b]個人好感度：[/b]（參考Affairs of Calradia）將原版遊戲中家族對家族的好感系統改為個人對個人，這樣你才可以完整體驗和每個NPC的關係互動。
[*][b]虛假消息：[/b]NPC可能會為了爭權奪利，或單純好玩？而散播謠言，小從替自家人編出好事，大到指控仇人下毒害死了人。被說的人可能出面否認，知道實情的人也可能出來澄清。
[*][b]自主的判斷：[/b]NPC會自行判斷相信與否，也會自行決定是否要把這個傳聞傳出去。在面對玩家時也會依照關係及個性決定是否要有所保留。
[*][b]紀事介面：[/b]Ctrl+L（預設，可自行修改）可以開啟紀事頁面，裡頭記載你所聽到的所有消息，並且當聽到相互矛盾的消息時，會標註「有矛盾」。如果想當個小偵探的話，記得時常查閱;)
[*][b]打聽系統：[/b]你可以詢問NPC一件你已經聽過的消息，看看對方有沒有不同面向的答案。或許你第一次聽到的其實不是真的？
[*][b]遊戲裡發生的事：[/b]遊戲中真正發生的事也會變成消息，例如被俘、獲釋、脫逃、出生、過世、婚事。
[*][b]各人有各人的說法：[/b]NPC說完消息會再添一句自己的看法。同一件事，當事人的朋友、仇人和不相干的人說法各不相同；當事人講自己的事，也會帶著自己的心情。
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]未來預計製作的機制[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]親身捲入：[/b]你可能會親眼目睹NPC之間的事件，甚至被捲入其中。
[*][b]更多的事件[/b]
[*][b]實際遊戲狀態改變：[/b]目前事件僅作為故事，除了好感之外的數值並不會有變動。未來希望可以加入聯動機制，讓這些事件變成「真的」。
[*][b]玩家也能開口：[/b]靠著三寸不爛之舌四處挑撥離間，讓整片大陸陷入混亂？你真是個壞分子;)
[*][b]更多消息來源：[/b]將不同模組的事件串接到本模組中。
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]安裝[/b][/color][/size]

[b]適用的遊戲版本：[/b]針對 [b]v1.4.8[/b] 建置，其他版本尚未測試。

[list=1]
[*]解壓縮後，將 VividWorld 整個資料夾置於遊戲的 Modules\ 目錄下。
[*][color=#D9534F][b]另需安裝 Mod Configuration Menu（MCM）[/b][/color]，並讓它排在本模組之前載入。
[*]於啟動器的模組清單中勾選 [b]Vivid World[/b]，順序置於 Native、SandBoxCore、Sandbox、StoryMode 之後。
[*]無須另行安裝 Harmony。
[/list]

[b]移除：[/b]刪除模組資料夾即可。建議刪除前先備份。


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]存檔安全[/b][/color][/size]

傳聞相關的資料[b]不寫入遊戲的存檔檔案[/b]，而是另存於
Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\VividWorld\

[list]
[*][b]移除模組後，既有存檔仍可正常讀取。[/b]「個人好感度」記下的每個人對你的好感會留在存檔裡，但原版遊戲不讀它，畫面回到同一家族共用族長的數字。
[*][b]將存檔移至另一台電腦時，傳聞資料不會隨之移轉[/b]，需一併複製上述資料夾。
[*][b]讀取較早的存檔時，傳聞也會跟著回到當時的狀態。[/b]每次存檔都會留一份傳聞快照；按 F9（預設，可自行修改）可以查看，並清掉存檔已刪除的那些快照。
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]相容性[/b][/color][/size]

[b]「平民不應與貴族攀談」一類的模組[/b]（例如 NaN、Lowborn）：本模組會偵測其存在，傳聞模式為「自動」時隨之改採寫實，將「主動詢問傳聞」限制於家族等級 1 以上。家族仍為等級 0 時問不到消息，此為刻意配合；若希望出身平民也能打聽，可改為暢玩。

[b]Calradia Remembers[/b]：本模組目前只針對 Calradia Remembers 做了串接。安裝後，與領主或流浪者用 AI 聊天時，他會知道自己在本模組裡聽過、至今還記得的傳聞——照他聽到的版本，也說得出是聽誰說的；已經忘記或早已過時的便不會再提。其他 AI 聊天模組目前還讀不到這些傳聞；未安裝時不影響本模組任何功能。交給 AI 模組的語言可在 MCM 的「AI 串接」選擇，預設為英文。

[b]接管對話開場白的模組[/b]：部分模組會完整接管領主的第一句話。遇此情形時，對話選單會多出一句「你剛才似乎欲言又止？」，供你把話題引回。

[b]Affairs of Calradia[/b]：它的「個人好感模式」開著時，做的是跟「個人好感度」同一件事，兩者不衝突；本模組偵測到它已在做，便不再重新分配好感。

除了「個人好感度」改變了遊戲計算「某人對你的好感」的方式之外，本模組不修改遊戲本身的 AI 決策，亦不覆寫任何原生檔案。


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]設定[/b][/color][/size]

[b]遊戲的設定畫面裡有一頁 Vivid World[/b]（由 Mod Configuration Menu 提供），直接在遊戲裡就能改。

設定檔位於 Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\VividWorld\config.json，首次啟動遊戲時自動產生，可調整總開關、熱鍵與快照保留份數等。兩邊改的是同一份檔案，選單上沒有的設定維持原樣。

[b]模組更新不會改動你既有的設定值[/b]，僅補上新版新增的鍵。


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]語言[/b][/color][/size]

目前支援英文、繁體中文與[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/13594]俄文[/url]，歡迎自行新增語言。
[list]
[*]感謝 Lingaraja 提供俄文翻譯！
[/list]


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]回報問題[/b][/color][/size]

日誌位於 Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\VividWorld\log.txt，回報時請一併附上。若問題與「誰向誰轉述了什麼」有關，請先將 config.json 中的 debug.logTellerTurns 設為 true，重啟遊戲後重現該情形，日誌會詳盡得多。


[size=4][color=#B8860B][b]附註[/b][/color][/size]

這是我的第一個騎砍mod，程式碼的撰寫完全使用AI(Claude)。如果有任何問題歡迎留言或是使用bug report機制。另外此mod完全開源，若是想要新增功能或提供意見，也歡迎到我的 [url=https://github.com/PH010546/VividWorld]github repo[/url]。謝謝！
